  "narrative": "No assessments are due. With validation budget exhausted, the next informative step is discovery-stage refinement of the conditional feature_063 pattern and confirmation of whether the two strong lowering markers, feature_037 and feature_027, retain their expected directions in one another's contexts. The first three proposals directly test the feature_063-by-marker conditioning inside feature_027=0, where the strongest validated feature_063 lowering evidence currently lies. A feature_063 simple contrast within feature_027=0/feature_002=0/feature_010=1 tests whether lowering persists when feature_010=1 is present but the raising marker feature_002 is absent; persistence would weaken a feature_010=0 dependence, while a weak or null contrast would support the current interpretation that feature_063 lowering is concentrated in feature_010=0 contexts. The feature_063-by-feature_010 interaction within feature_027=0/feature_002=0 is registered in the positive direction because a positive raw interaction means the raw feature_063 exposed-minus-comparator contrast is higher, i.e. less lowering or reversal, in feature_010=1 than in the feature_010=0 complement. This is the expected pattern if feature_010 status explains the attenuation of feature_063 lowering. The feature_063-by-feature_002 interaction within feature_027=0/feature_010=0 is registered in the negative direction because the prior nested feature_002=1 simple contrast, although not independently validated in a related broader context, was numerically more lowering than the feature_002=0 contrast; a negative raw interaction would mean feature_002=1 amplifies feature_063 lowering rather than attenuating it. The next two simple feature_063 contrasts test context boundaries more directly: feature_027=0/feature_010=0/feature_037=1 tests whether the feature_063 signal extends into the feature_037=1 context when feature_010=0 is retained, while feature_027=0/feature_010=0/feature_002=1/feature_037=0 tests whether the unstable feature_002=1 context becomes more interpretable after removing the strong feature_037 lowering stratum. Finally, the feature_037 contrast within feature_027=1 tests whether the accepted feature_037 lowering association remains present among feature_027=1 participants, where ceiling-floor or marker-overlap attenuation is a plausible alternative. The feature_002-by-feature_010 interaction within feature_027=0/feature_037=0 tests whether the positive raw interaction between the two raising markers persists in the largest clean marker-free-lower setting after excluding the feature_027 and feature_037 lowering strata that may have diluted the broader interaction. All proposals are unadjusted association tests in the supplied dataset and do not establish causality or generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 explore update. No due assessments. Current supported dataset-specific associations: feature_037=1 lowers outcome_001 by about 0.80 units; feature_027=1 lowers by about 0.81 units; feature_002=1 raises by about 0.80 units; feature_010=1 raises by about 0.40 units. Feature_063 is conditional, strongest and independently validated in feature_027=0 and especially the nested feature_027=0/feature_037=0/feature_002=0/feature_010=0 context; feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 contexts have been weak, unstable, or failed independent validation. No validation budget remains, so new work is discovery-only. New proposals refine feature_063 conditioning inside feature_027=0: simple lowering in 002=0/010=1, 063-by-010 interaction in 002=0, reversed 063-by-002 interaction in 010=0, simple lowering in 010=0/037=1, and simple lowering in 010=0/002=1/037=0. They also test feature_037 lowering among feature_027=1 participants and feature_002-by-feature_010 interaction among feature_027=0/feature_037=0 participants. If feature_063 lowering persists in 002=0/010=1, its feature_010 dependence is weaker than currently favored. If a positive 063-by-010 interaction validates or strongly clears threshold, feature_010=0 should be retained in the main feature_063 context. If a negative 063-by-002 interaction is supported, the prior interpretation of feature_002 attenuation should be revised toward enhancement. The feature_037-in-feature_027=1 test checks whether the two strong lowering markers are approximately independent in extreme contexts. The feature_002-by-feature_010 test checks marker synergy in the cleaner feature_027=0/feature_037=0 population. All conclusions remain unadjusted associations in the supplied dataset."
